speechtext:
Mr. Chairman, I want to take this opportunity of congratulating labour unions in my riding, and the Catholic unions, on their invaluable services to workers. I must also point out the part played in Joli-ette by the local Labour Council.
I call upon the government:
(1)	To appoint labour representatives on all councils or boards set up to consider matters of concern to workers;
(2)	To consider the possibility of extending unemployment insurance benefits to farm workers;
(3)	To continue to vote millions of dollars for housing developments and, if possible, to broaden the scope of the National Housing Act so that all workers may become home owners;
(4)	To maintain restrictions on immigration;
(5)	To permanently reject the proposal of free trade with the United Kingdom, as it would put 300,000 workers out of work;
(6)	To diversify our trade;
(7)	To avoid credit restrictions;
(8)	To enact, if possible, at some time, legislation forbidding employers to refuse hiring of workers aged 45 or more.
